<!--Post: 5009--><!--Time: 1106849104-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5009"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George has been fighting thoughtout the entire board with getting this information straight.  We have no conclusive legal evidence to say BTK killed these women ... <BR> <BR>well we don&#39;t ... I have no idea what the WPD has ... or even Tom ... <BR> <BR>Regardless, as INVESTIGATORS, even amateur, we need to realize that Hedge and Davis are unsolved cases that have no links to BTK except the weird vague relation of a brick.  NO CONNECTION WHATSOEVER! <BR> <BR>Now there is THEORY.  And many of us, convinced that BTK will once again drop a bombsell like he did with Vicki,  theorize that the packages #7 and #8 contain information on these two cases.   <BR> <BR>Its an interesting Theory, but it needs proof and evidence.  We don&#39;t have that.  We need to have that before Tom is convinced enough to actually make a &#34;Definite Victim: NAME&#34; section. <BR> <BR>This isn&#39;t a rant.  This is just a reminder that as investigators we need to find the evidence, not the speculations.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5009-->
<!--Post: 5030--><!--Time: 1106854192-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5030"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 11:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/10745102.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/10745102.htm</a> <BR>Posted on Thu, Jan. 27, 2005  <BR>POSSIBLE BTK CONNECTIONS  <BR>== <BR>POSSIBLE BTK CONNECTIONS <BR> <BR>April 27, 1985 -- Park City resident Marine Hedge is abducted. Her car is found May 2 at 21st and Woodlawn; her purse is found May 5 near 143rd East and 37th North; her body is found May 5, 1985, near 53rd North and Webb Road. <BR> <BR>Jan. 19, 1991 -- Delores Davis abducted from her home one-half mile east of Park City. Her body is found Feb. 1, 1991, near 117th North and Meridian. <BR>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
